I wonder if we need to export the values ourselves at all here.

`assertSame()` already knows how to display the expected/actual values, including arrays and objects. Could we keep the custom message focused on identifying the event/key and let PHPUnit display the actual difference?

Something like:

```php
self::assertSame(
    $value,
    $this->payload[$key],
    sprintf('The event "%s" data "%s" is different than expected.', $this->eventName, $key),
);
```

This would fix the original issue without introducing/duplicating our own value exporter.
